        { "feature": "Legend items that hide and show an item's slices in every ring", "noscript": "none" },
        { "feature": "A table of each ring's values and shares in a \"Show data\" disclosure" },
        { "feature": "Tooltips on hover and from the keyboard, along a ring and between rings", "noscript": "none" }
      ],
      "examples": [
        { "id": "nested-donut-chart-usage", "title": "This year against last", "lead": "Give `NestedDonutChart` the `Items`, each slice's name as `Argument`, and a `DonutRing` for each measure, with its `Value` and `Name`. The first ring is the outer one, and each item keeps its color in every ring.", "after": ["Rings compare poorly: the same share is a longer arc on the outer ring than on the inner one. To compare how two wholes split, a `Chart` with `Stacking=\"ChartStacking.Percent\"` and bars across reads better. Use rings when the donut's look matters more, for two measures, at most three.", "The line under the title names each ring by its place."],
          "notes": { "noscript": "There are no tooltips. Each slice still shows its ring, value and share on hover, and Show data lists them all." } }
